                <pb facs="0572" n="554" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v12p1/pg554"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">790.5/6–1454 (Bulky)</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Report of the Five-Power Military Conference of June
                        3–11, 1954</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d219-f1"/></head>
                <note rend="inline" type="source">[Extracts]</note>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-06-11">June 11, 1954</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Five Power Military Conference Of
                        June 1954</hi></p>
                <p>In accordance with instructions, the Military Representatives of Australia,
                    France, New Zealand, the United Kingdom and the United States met in Washington
                    from 3rd to 11th of June, 1954, to consider the military situation in South East
                    Asia.</p>
                <p>The Report of this Five Power Military Conference is attached.</p>
                <closer><signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>S[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ydney</hi>] F. <hi
                                    rendition="#small-caps">Rowell</hi><lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                    >Lt. General<lb/>Australia</hi></item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">J.E. Valluy</hi><lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Général de Corps
                                d’Armée<lb/>France</hi></item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">W.G. Gentry</hi><lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Major General<lb/>New Zealand</hi></item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Harding</hi><lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Field Marshal<lb/>United Kingdom</hi></item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">R.B. Carney</hi><lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Admiral<lb/>United States</hi></item>
                        </list>
                    </signed></closer>







